{"id":"por-t0-0015","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":3,"text_native":"Aceita euros? (uh-SAY-tuh EHW-roosh?, /ɐ.ˈsɐj.tɐ ˈew.ɾuʃ/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do you accept euros?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking what something costs, and what you think of the price. Every transaction needs both.","caution":"Prices are often negotiable in a market and fixed in a shop. Asking what you think of it reads differently in each.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
