{"id":"por-t0-0042","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":8,"text_native":"Quanto custa isto? (KWUHN-too KOOSH-tuh EESH-too, /ˈkwɐ̃.tu ˈkuʃ.tɐ ˈiʃ.tu/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"How much is this?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Prices, sizes, and declining politely when you are not buying.","caution":"Deciding not to buy is a normal part of shopping and saying so early is easier than walking away.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0043","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":8,"text_native":"É demasiado caro. (EH d(ih)-muh-zee-AH-do KER-roo, /ˈɛ dɨ.mɐ.zi.ˈa.du ˈka.ɾu/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"That's too expensive","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Prices, sizes, and declining politely when you are not buying.","caution":"Deciding not to buy is a normal part of shopping and saying so early is easier than walking away.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0044","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":8,"text_native":"caro (KAH-roo, /ˈka.ɾu/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"expensive","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Prices, sizes, and declining politely when you are not buying.","caution":"Deciding not to buy is a normal part of shopping and saying so early is easier than walking away.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0045","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":8,"text_native":"barato (buh-RAH-too, /bɐ.ˈɾa.tu/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Prices, sizes, and declining politely when you are not buying.","caution":"Deciding not to buy is a normal part of shopping and saying so early is easier than walking away.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0046","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":8,"text_native":"Não quero isso. (nuhnw KEH-roo EE-soo, /ˈnɐ̃w ˈkɛ.ɾu ˈi.su/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I don't want it","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Prices, sizes, and declining politely when you are not buying.","caution":"Deciding not to buy is a normal part of shopping and saying so early is easier than walking away.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0047","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":8,"text_native":"Estás a enganar-me. (sh-TAHZ uh een-guh-NAHR-m(ih), /ʃ.ˈtaz ɐ ẽ.gɐ.ˈnaɾ-mɨ/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"You're cheating me","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Prices, sizes, and declining politely when you are not buying.","caution":"Deciding not to buy is a normal part of shopping and saying so early is easier than walking away.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0048","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":10,"text_native":"Deixe-me em paz! (DAY-sh(ih)-m(ih) ehm pahsh!, /ˈdɐj.ʃɨ mɨ ɐ̃j ˈpaʃ/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Leave me alone!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying that something is wrong, and understanding when it is wrong with you.","caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0049","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":10,"text_native":"Não me toque! (nuhnw m(ih) TOH-k(ih)!, /ˈnɐ̃w mɨ ˈto.kɨ/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying that something is wrong, and understanding when it is wrong with you.","caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0050","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":10,"text_native":"Vou chamar a polícia. (voh shuh-MAHR uh poo-LEE-see-uh, /ˈvo ʃɐ.ˈmaɾ ɐ pu.ˈɫi.sɨ.ɐ/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I'll call the police","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying that something is wrong, and understanding when it is wrong with you.","caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0051","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":10,"text_native":"Polícia! (poo-LEE-see-uh, /pu.ˈɫi.sɨ.ɐ/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Police!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying that something is wrong, and understanding when it is wrong with you.","caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"por-t0-0052","lang":"por","tier":0,"domain":10,"text_native":"Pára! Ladrão! (PAH-ruh luh-DRUHNW, /ˈpa.ɾɐ ɫɐ.ˈdɾɐ̃w/)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Stop! Thief!","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Signs on doors and shopfronts. You read these rather than say them, and misreading one puts you on the wrong side of a door.","caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Portuguese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Portuguese%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
